    "body": "I thought you were talking about Fetch never queuing tasks for transmitted bytes (since that's streams now).\r\n\r\nFramed like this I understand the issue better. It's the invocation of HTTP-redirect fetch by HTML's navigate that causes a problem. And when HTML navigate invokes it, the recursive flag should probably not be set, since it's not really recursive and we're not following redirects.",
